              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imperītus, imperīta, imperītum — \"inexperienced, unskilled\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperītus nauta nāvem frēgit. The unskilled sailor wrecked the ship."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imperītus, imperīta, imperītum: the opposite of the word for experienced, with in-, not. With the genitive: bellī imperītus, without experience of war."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imperītus is built from in- \"not\" and perītus \"experienced\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), which comes from the root of experior \"to try, to test\"."
            }
          ]
        },
